{
 "what_you_observe": [
  "Tuesday, February 2. Seven pm.",
  "Phil plays the last eight bars until he can get through them.",
  "Rita said in the lobby: Alma, your daughter wants your voice. Talk to her.",
  "Larry said in the lobby: I don't turn back to the lobby. But I say, low, to the nearest one of them, the one who's still holding a saucer: 'Rialto's closing. I'm going to get a shot before the lights go out. Be back for the party.' It's not a question. I'm already walking.",
  "You are now at ballroom.",
  "There is time for one evening visit. The ballroom lights are on and the station line is open."
 ],
 "your_own_memories": [
  {
   "when": "last Tuesday afternoon",
   "witnessed": "Phil uses the paid ticket and rides the coach all the way to Pittsburgh.."
  },
  {
   "when": "last evening in Pittsburgh",
   "witnessed": "You reached your sister from the terminal payphone. She confirmed the van booking for Wednesday.",
   "your_words": "Hey, it's Phil. I'm in Pittsburgh now, just off the coach. Listen, about tomorrow—van's booked for the couch, right? I want to nail down the pickup time and make sure I know which hallway we're dragging it through. I'll be at your place by noon, tops."
  },
  {
   "when": "this morning",
   "witnessed": "After that evening in Pittsburgh you woke back in your hotel bed. The radio again announced Tuesday, February 2."
  },
  {
   "what_you_did": "Phil plays the last eight bars until he can get through them.",
   "what_you_said": "\"Give me the afternoon. I'll be back by five. And Larry—don't let anyone book the ballroom for a corporate thing. I need that piano at eight.\"",
   "your_intention": "The driver can find the jack. The Rialto will close. The coach will sit in the lot. I already took that route last Tuesday—boarded, rode, called my sister, confirmed the van, said the right words, and woke up in this bed with the radio telling me it's Tuesday again. Reaching Pittsburgh didn't do it. So I'm not boarding the coach.\n\nMy theory, untested: the loop breaks the way it breaks in the film. Not by going somewhere. By *being* here, doing the work with my hands, playing the same eight bars until they aren't the same eight bars anymore. The ending isn't a destination. It's a Tuesday where I'm at the piano and I'm not performing for a camera and I'm not selling a forecast. I'm just a man learning a tune in a ballroom that smells like old carpet and lemon polish.\n\nIf I play that set tonight, and Rita hears me, and I'm not the weatherman on the screen—then maybe Wednesday is the thing that comes after. I don't know. I haven't tested it. But it's the only act I've got that matches the ending I'm trying to reach, and it's the one I can do with my hands right now, in this room, where the keys are cold and the light is going gold."
  },
  "Phil plays the last eight bars until he can get through them.",
  "Rita said in the lobby: Alma, your daughter wants your voice. Talk to her.",
  "Larry said in the lobby: I don't turn back to the lobby. But I say, low, to the nearest one of them, the one who's still holding a saucer: 'Rialto's closing. I'm going to get a shot before the lights go out. Be back for the party.' It's not a question. I'm already walking.",
  "You are now at ballroom."
 ],
 "who_you_are_with": "your present location",
 "physical_choices": {
  "play_piano": "Play at the ballroom, whether anyone comes or not.",
  "go_to_party": "Attend the party and see who else comes.",
  "ask_Rita_to_dance": "Go to the ballroom and offer Rita a dance. Her choice determines whether she is there and available.",
  "wait_at_Rialto": "Spend the evening at the Rialto booth.",
  "go_to_bed": "Go upstairs alone and let the evening go by.",
  "sit_at_depot": "Let the evening go by on the empty depot bench."
 }
}
